@using LineOps.Desk.Primitives

@*
    What a snippet shows when its load failed: the sentence naming what did not load, and the
    key that loads it again.

    LoadFailure's job at row scale. A panel's failure is the Error kind of EmptyState, a block
    with room around it; a snippet is a few lines under a grid row, so it keeps the warning
    note it always used and carries the key inside it, Plain and small, at the line's end.

    The key is the only retry a snippet has. A row's views are a segmented control, and
    pressing the chosen segment again does nothing, so a sentence ending "Try again." named an
    action the row no longer offered. The sentence now says only what did not load; the key
    says what to do.

    Clicks stop here. The strip and the Board's hosted child row already stop a click inside
    them before it reaches the grid row, which opens the game; this stops its own as well, so a
    snippet hosted somewhere without that guard cannot open a window by asking to load again.
*@

<div @onclick:stopPropagation="true">
    <Note State="DeskState.Warning" Style="margin:0">
        <DeskRow Justify="DeskJustify.Between">
            <span>@Message</span>
            <DeskButton Size="DeskKeySize.Small" Emphasis="DeskEmphasis.Plain"
                        Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.Refresh" OnClick="Retry">
                Try again
            </DeskButton>
        </DeskRow>
    </Note>
</div>

@code {
    /// <summary>What did not load, as a sentence: "The market did not load."</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public string? Message { get; set; }

    /// <summary>The snippet's own load, run again. A callback, so the snippet re-renders as it settles.</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public EventCallback OnRetry { get; set; }

    private Task Retry() => OnRetry.InvokeAsync();
}
